The class `ScheduledDirectTask` is a thin wrapper that delegates to a provided `Runnable` and handles thread bookkeeping and error propagation. Its behavior is trivial and its performance is dominated by the wrapped `Runnable`, not by any internal logic. Benchmarking this class in isolation would not provide meaningful insights, as the measured cost would be negligible and highly dependent on external code. Therefore, a JMH benchmark is unnecessary.